Now that we're waiting for the "is closed" log, can we move the `requestUnblocked.SetResult();` so it's called before stopServerTask completes?

```
cts.Cancel();
await closedMessageTask;
requestUnblocked.SetResult();
await stopServerTask;
```

This test doesn't need to block the request until after the abort times out. Waiting for the abort to start (which is done by `await closedMessageTask`) should be enough.
